    Remove duplicate Jackson bundles from the distributions (#8223)
    
    CXF's cxf-jackson feature, pulled in by cxf-jaxrs, installs its own
    Jackson 2.22.1 bundles (core, databind, dataformat-yaml,
    datatype-jsr310, jaxrs-base, jaxrs-json-provider) next to our
    ${jackson.version}. Karaf's spring-legacy features additionally put core
    and databind 2.22.2 into system/. Since the resolver prefers the highest
    version, nothing was wired to these except CXF's
    jackson-datatype-jsr310, which swagger-core used. They were dead weight
    (about 4.8 MB) and made security scanners report old Jackson versions.
    
    Blacklist all Jackson 2 bundles older than ${jackson.version} in the
    assembly. The plugin also writes the blacklist to
    etc/org.apache.karaf.features.xml, so it applies at runtime as well.
    jackson-annotations is left out because its version (2.22) would match
    the range. Since our jackson-datatype-jsr310 was only a dependency
    bundle of opencast-graphql-tp, add it to ext-core so swagger-core still
    resolves.
    
    Each Jackson artifact is now shipped and installed exactly once (8
    instead of 13 bundles in dist-develop).
    
    This is part of https://github.com/opencast/opencast/issues/8214
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    - Build and run Opencast.
    - Look at the installed bundles in the Karaf console
    
